Primary: `REGLEMENT_WORK.md` (source of truth). Follow it over verbose default agent habits.

Hard rules:
- Token/command/file-read economy without losing quality.
- Goal in 1–2 sentences → plan 3–6 bullets → one verified step at a time.
- Read/search only what the next step requires. No broad repo/home scans, no full log dumps.
- Short replies: done → result → more needed yes/no.
- Before first write: minimal inspect + recoverable checkpoint.
- After UI/code change: checks from the reglement (typecheck / dev / UI).
- No Electron/UI/preload rewrites "for beauty" without a proven bug and user OK.
- Safety (checkpoint, evidence, no destructive git) is never skipped.
